guide forever/professions/camping
title Camping
category Professions
keywords camping, campfire, Basic Campfire Kit, Camp Benefits, camp item, Lodestone, Incense Candle, Camp Chair, Camp Tent, Mana Well, Sharpening Wheel, Enchanted Lute, Reagent Bot, Faction Banner, First Aid Kit, Fish Bowl, blueprint, Camping 101, The Great Outdoors
collects 279981
why A campfire, your profession's camp item and an hour of Camp Benefits.
levels 1-60
zone Stormwind City
next forever/miscellaneous/cozy-sleeping-bag

# Camping is Forever's own: someone places a campfire, everyone near it may place one camp item of
# their own profession, and sitting by the fire for about a minute gives Camp Benefits, one buff for an
# hour with what every camp item there adds. A camp item buff is a weaker form of a class buff and does
# not stack with it. Each player places one camp item; placing it starts an hour before the next.
#
# The campfire comes with Cooking: the Basic Campfire Kit (1 Simple Wood, Cooking 1) holds three camp
# items. The Journeyman Campfire Kit (Cooking 90, 1 Star Wood) holds five; its blueprint drops from Lord
# Serpentis in Wailing Caverns. The Expert Campfire Kit (learned at Cooking 200, used from 220, 1 Thick
# Logs) holds ten; its blueprint drops from Slavecrusher Grox in Krol'dok Stronghold.
#
# Every profession's first camp item is taught by its trainer from skill 20 (this guide's steps show
# only those of the professions you have at 20). The starting areas' Camping 101 quests teach the same
# recipe for free; the buffs work without them. Better camp items come from blueprints that bosses drop:
# Fermenter (Rath'mael), Alchemy Laboratory (Ras Frostwhisper), Anvil (Gilnid), Master Forge (Golem Lord
# Argelmach), Arcane Salvager (Shade of the Archmage), Arcane Forge (Nanaya), Repair Bot (Sneed),
# Anarchist's Workbench (Ezra Grimm), Tanning Rack (Razorclaw the Butcher), Sewing Machine (Vectus),
# Spinning Wheel (Unstable Sentinel), Loom (Baroness Anastari), Greenhouse (Shadetooth), Seed Hybridizer
# (Tendris Warpwood), Rock Garden (Relic Guardian), Molten Foundry (Ambassador Flamelash), Field Guide
# (Lady Anacondra) and Trapper's Workbench (Houndmaster Loksey or The Beast). Each also gives its
# profession's first camp item buff.
#
# Item, recipe and blueprint ids, reagents and drops: data/forever (professions.json, items.json).
# Camp Benefits is the client's spell 1229741. The Cozy Sleeping Bag guide is offered when this one ends.

step Learn Cooking
  tip The Basic Campfire Kit comes with Cooking at skill 1. No character level needed.
  train Cooking Apprentice

step Buy 5 Simple Wood
  tip One Simple Wood makes one Basic Campfire Kit.
  buy 4470 x5 nearest

step Craft 5 Basic Campfire Kits
  tip Kits stack in one bag slot, and friends can use the spares.
  craft 1229737 x5

step Learn Mana Well
  tip Your Alchemy trainer teaches this camp item from Alchemy skill 20.
  when skill Alchemy 20
